{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle","id":1111333,"title":"Ordo Dracul Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-04T10:28:30-07:00","id":1111333,"title":"Ordo Dracul Chronicle","content":"I'm going to be running a single covenant game within the near future, and most of my players are leaning towards the Ordo Dracul at the moment. We will be using second edition vampire rules, and I was wondering what books from 1e I should make use of (if any).<br /> <br /> Also, should I allow the common coils only (Wyrm, Voivode, and Ascendant) when it comes to the begunning of the Chronicle, and let them learn the more esoteric coils (Zirnitra, Ziva, and Quintessence) later on in the game.<br /> <br /> Also, can people help me with some ideas on how to design Elder coils and scales for each of the mysteries, like how Quintessence is part of the Voivode mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T11:46:21-07:00","id":1111370,"title":"","content":"I think the Ordo Dracul book still has a lot of good setting material, even if the crunch is dated (though the...alchemy Discipline whose name I can't recall might be a good place to mine for Scale inspiration).<br /> <br /> If you want the chronicle to have a higher weirdness quotient, let them take whatever Coils they like; if you want it to be more mysterious, limit the Coils to those in the core at first. Alternatively, if you want to inject a little paranoia between Dragon characters, let players take their Coils privately (whatever they want), and then let them lie about it in-character (if they want).<br /> <br /> As for Elder Coils, I feel like the design principle is that it should expand the scope of the theme...so, an Elder Coil of the Wyrm might let the vampire extend her will over the Beast into a physical manifestation? An Elder Coil of the Ascendant probably doesn't let you walk in sunlight, but maybe it obviates things like Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:38:22-07:00","id":1111485,"title":"","content":"Spoiling is the alchemy discipline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T05:25:00-07:00","id":1111620,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, a bit hard to make an Ordo centered game, it would be much easier to play Invictus for example, considering that their inner politics are a shark pit already.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest if you burrow some themes from the Tremere Clan in the classic WoD: Darwinism, rigid hierarchy and maybe some inner covenant backstabbing and &quot;getting rid&quot; of your fellow dragons to leave room for advancing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T06:27:45-07:00","id":1111633,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on the Ordo only game:<br /> <br /> ~ Nail down how Wyrm Nests work. This is going to be a huge part of your game. You'll want scenes that revolve around using them. <br /> <br /> ~ Figure out how much of a social challenge you want the Ordo to have. In a regular game, the Ordo Dracul serve as a kind of wild-card in the standard Invictus v. Carthian, Lance v. Circle standoff. In a pure Ordo game, the socialization tends to take a back seat to being vampire-mage types. No, they don't get the magic, but they do have the curiosity. Most of the different social challenges the Ordo Dracul face tend to revolve around getting access to a Wyrm's Nest, be they a social challenge, or a physical one. <br /> <br /> ~ Make sure to leave lots of room for Sworn of the Axe types and Sworn of the Mystery types. The stereotypical Dragon is going to be an investigative Dying Light type. Try and branch out to make sure you've got lots of things for everyone. Its very easy to do an underground fighting ring in a Wyrm's Nest for the sworn of the axe. That's part of what they do. Nailing down some Sworn of the Mysteries plots for PCs are going to be a bit trickier. <br /> <br /> ~ The Coil of the Quintessence admits to being part of the Mystery of the Voivode. Think about possibly tying Zirnitra, Ziva to the other Mysteries as well as if they were &quot;advanced&quot; coils. This way, you can also keep a bit of the themes of turning Beast, Stasis and Blood on each other to grow (as per Rites of the Dragon fiction). This also makes using the Ordo Dracul titles slightly easier to use as well.<br /> <br /> ~ There's lots of rumors about Dracula, two of his missing brides, the Unholy, and more. Think about bringing in some of these rumors and cult-of-personality worship. <br /> <br /> ~ Keep a close eye on what psychic powers you bring in. Its very easy for Zirnitra to become the uber-coil, and have psychic powers replace disciplines and do everything that way. I know of a number of games that just flat out banned Zirnitra because of how quickly it went off the rails. <br /> <br /> ~ Potentially think about devising some Coils or Scales or abilities for dealing with ghosts, or how regular disciplines interact. The Ordo v. haunted house is a pretty common plot. <br /> <br /> ~ Other potential plot include investigating the Jaing Shi or other Night Horror: Wicked Dead alternate vampires. There's hints of the Jiang Shi in core book, and we're getting some more on dhampir in the upcoming ghoul book. Have fun with non-Kindred vampire types popping up to investigate. Think about awarding blood beats for finding them and using them as part of the Ordo Dracul's attempts to learn coils / scales (see core book for more info on blood beats).<br /> <br /> ~ Strix. Many don't like them, but the Ordo Dracul is ripe for bringing them in as &quot;demons.&quot; By demons, I mean to make deals for information / mystic ability, for temptation, and more. The Ordo Dracul have a proscritption against becoming the servant of an angel or demon, and the strix are perfect to fit that place. Its also possible to bring in hints of the Belial's Brood in with the strix, perhaps making up Vestments that could be mistaken for Coils as part of the slippery slide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:25:31-07:00","id":1111774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111633#post1111633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts on the Ordo only game:<br /> <br /> ~ Nail down how Wyrm Nests work. This is going to be a huge part of your game. You'll want scenes that revolve around using them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to figure out how Wyrm's Nests work in general, so any help there is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Figure out how much of a social challenge you want the Ordo to have. In a regular game, the Ordo Dracul serve as a kind of wild-card in the standard Invictus v. Carthian, Lance v. Circle standoff. In a pure Ordo game, the socialization tends to take a back seat to being vampire-mage types. No, they don't get the magic, but they do have the curiosity. Most of the different social challenges the Ordo Dracul face tend to revolve around getting access to a Wyrm's Nest, be they a social challenge, or a physical one. </div> </div> </div>I plan to have both physical and social challenges for the Wyrm's Nests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Make sure to leave lots of room for Sworn of the Axe types and Sworn of the Mystery types. The stereotypical Dragon is going to be an investigative Dying Light type. Try and branch out to make sure you've got lots of things for everyone. Its very easy to do an underground fighting ring in a Wyrm's Nest for the sworn of the axe. That's part of what they do. Nailing down some Sworn of the Mysteries plots for PCs are going to be a bit trickier. </div> </div> </div>I actually have a group that will probably be spread amongst the Sworn groups, so I'm pretty excited for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ The Coil of the Quintessence admits to being part of the Mystery of the Voivode. Think about possibly tying Zirnitra, Ziva to the other Mysteries as well as if they were &amp;quot;advanced&amp;quot; coils. This way, you can also keep a bit of the themes of turning Beast, Stasis and Blood on each other to grow (as per Rites of the Dragon fiction). This also makes using the Ordo Dracul titles slightly easier to use as well. </div> </div> </div>I could see tying Zirnitra to the Mystery of the Ascendant, but that leaves the Mystery of the Wyrm without an advanced coil, unless the Coil of Ziva would be a study of dichotomy for that mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ There's lots of rumors about Dracula, two of his missing brides, the Unholy, and more. Think about bringing in some of these rumors and cult-of-personality worship. </div> </div> </div>These are some interesting ideas, I'll have to make use of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Keep a close eye on what psychic powers you bring in. Its very easy for Zirnitra to become the uber-coil, and have psychic powers replace disciplines and do everything that way. I know of a number of games that just flat out banned Zirnitra because of how quickly it went off the rails. </div> </div> </div>I was worried about that, so I'll probably leave that as a coil to learn later on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Potentially think about devising some Coils or Scales or abilities for dealing with ghosts, or how regular disciplines interact. The Ordo v. haunted house is a pretty common plot. </div> </div> </div>I had plans to make use of the mortal books abjuration system, and using dirge for the virtue analogue and mask for the vice analogue. I was also planning to have auspex one being able to reveal ghosts and spirits, and if the character was aware of a ghost the discipline would work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Other potential plot include investigating the Jaing Shi or other Night Horror: Wicked Dead alternate vampires. There's hints of the Jiang Shi in core book, and we're getting some more on dhampir in the upcoming ghoul book. Have fun with non-Kindred vampire types popping up to investigate. Think about awarding blood beats for finding them and using them as part of the Ordo Dracul's attempts to learn coils / scales (see core book for more info on blood beats). </div> </div> </div>I had some plans for this, but thinks for reminding me of Clan Jiang-Shi. I like the blood beats idea as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Strix. Many don't like them, but the Ordo Dracul is ripe for bringing them in as &amp;quot;demons.&amp;quot; By demons, I mean to make deals for information / mystic ability, for temptation, and more. The Ordo Dracul have a proscritption against becoming the servant of an angel or demon, and the strix are perfect to fit that place. Its also possible to bring in hints of the Belial's Brood in with the strix, perhaps making up Vestments that could be mistaken for Coils as part of the slippery slide. </div> </div> </div>I actually love the Strix; the image of shadowy owls in the night always felt primordial to me, and I enjoyed that aspect of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:17:50-07:00","id":1111806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111620#post1111620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, a bit hard to make an Ordo centered game, it would be much easier to play Invictus for example, considering that their inner politics are a shark pit already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sady, most of my group aren't the biggest fans of the Invictus; their toys aren't big and flashy, and they aren't big fans of aristrocacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd suggest if you burrow some themes from the Tremere Clan in the classic WoD: Darwinism, rigid hierarchy and maybe some inner covenant backstabbing and &amp;quot;getting rid&amp;quot; of your fellow dragons to leave room for advancing? </div> </div> </div>I'll have to do some reading on the Tremere again, but I'll be sure to take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:29:31-07:00","id":1111813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111774#post1111774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am trying to figure out how Wyrm's Nests work in general, so any help there is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. At the most basic, &quot;wyrm nest&quot; is just a fancy phrase for generic &quot;place of power.&quot; Most commonly enough, people tend to use a bit of crossover - ley line nodes/hallows, spirit locus or haunted houses. <br /> <br /> Once you have the location, something about it somehow makes it easier to develop a coil when you perform a certain kind of &quot;ritual.&quot; Back in 1e, when we had Buddhist and mesmerism as methods of learning the Coils, I just used whatever resonance was appropriate and said it happened. Now? The Ordo Dracul is absolutely more blood alchemy / pseudo-science-medice based as a whole instead. So, I tend to propose using the equivalent of tass in each location. I don't know if you're familiar with the idea, but tass is a concept in Mage that, somehow, mana takes on physical form. This can be as a sacred spring that, when drunk, gives you mana, or perhaps an aloe plant you use to rub on your skin, etc. <br /> <br /> What this means for the Ordo Dracul? I personally run things such that the Wyrm Nests always have some kind of physical manifestation of the place's energy, and the Defiant take said manifestation, crush it up with blood, and ... apply it somehow. Bath, drink, etc. Drug treatments, in short.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:31:50-07:00","id":1111816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111806#post1111806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sady, most of my group aren't the biggest fans of the Invictus; their toys aren't big and flashy, and they aren't big fans of aristrocacy.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're thinking of the 1e version. 2e are more organized crime mixed with big businesses than royalty now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll have to do some reading on the Tremere again, but I'll be sure to take a look. </div> </div> </div>Take care you don't accidentily remove the actual Ordo Dracul's organization, though. The Tremere are a pyramid, but the Ordo is a winding mix of several different paths; rigid hierarchy it is not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:54:36-07:00","id":1111823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111813#post1111813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure. At the most basic, &amp;quot;wyrm nest&amp;quot; is just a fancy phrase for generic &amp;quot;place of power.&amp;quot; Most commonly enough, people tend to use a bit of crossover - ley line nodes/hallows, spirit locus or haunted houses. <br /> <br /> Once you have the location, something about it somehow makes it easier to develop a coil when you perform a certain kind of &amp;quot;ritual.&amp;quot; Back in 1e, when we had Buddhist and mesmerism as methods of learning the Coils, I just used whatever resonance was appropriate and said it happened. Now? The Ordo Dracul is absolutely more blood alchemy / pseudo-science-medice based as a whole instead. So, I tend to propose using the equivalent of tass in each location. I don't know if you're familiar with the idea, but tass is a concept in Mage that, somehow, mana takes on physical form. This can be as a sacred spring that, when drunk, gives you mana, or perhaps an aloe plant you use to rub on your skin, etc. <br /> <br /> What this means for the Ordo Dracul? I personally run things such that the Wyrm Nests always have some kind of physical manifestation of the place's energy, and the Defiant take said manifestation, crush it up with blood, and ... apply it somehow. Bath, drink, etc. Drug treatments, in short.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've played a bit of mage, so I know about Tass a little bit. That's probably a good way to work with it; most of the answers I've gotten about it in the past haven't really helped. So, should I check the Ordo Dracul book put for the alchemy part, because I don't remember it being described all that much in the we core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:59:04-07:00","id":1111825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111816#post1111816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're thinking of the 1e version. 2e are more organized crime mixed with big businesses than royalty now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know; I've always run them as a bit of a mix. Some domains lead towards the aristrocacy titles, and other domains mostly just use them as titles and act more organized crime and big business. I like to have a healthy mix of both though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take care you don't accidentily remove the actual Ordo Dracul's organization, though. The Tremere are a pyramid, but the Ordo is a winding mix of several different paths; rigid hierarchy it is not. </div> </div> </div>I've always had my Ordo Dracul typically act more like a selfish scientific community; they'll share some of the information amongst each other, and then there are labs, field work, and mentor/apprentices. However, they typically keep the best stuff for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:58:36-07:00","id":1111912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111806#post1111806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, most of my group aren't the biggest fans of the Invictus; their toys aren't big and flashy, and they aren't big fans of aristrocacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think having the right contacts, allies and resources and even a few well-placed Oaths here and there beat any Coil or Scale the dragons can come up with. After all, it's much more spectacular and satisfying when you can pull off a political maneuver or win a fight using mundane tools (and Disciplines) over fancy special powers, but that's just my opinion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:14:39-07:00","id":1112037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1111823#post1111823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played a bit of mage, so I know about Tass a little bit. That's probably a good way to work with it; most of the answers I've gotten about it in the past haven't really helped.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, its always been extremely vague and hand waved. Details sorely lacking. There's really no answer, because its always been kind of open ended. 1e did have the Wyrm Nest rituals, but that was basically stealing mage-like rituals, adapting them, shoving the energy into a human, then eating the human. You could probably make a Scale to do the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, should I check the Ordo Dracul book put for the alchemy part, because I don't remember it being described all that much in the we core book. </div> </div> </div> Not really there either. When I say alchemy, I'm just talking about how scales work, and the focus on pseudo-scientific processes that the Ordo use. When using a scale, you create a mixture of blood and other chemicals and inject it, or bathe in it, etc. Or you use sleep deprivation with sun lamps. Etc. Its all coated with a veneer of mystical-science mix. Alchemy is the most familiar term I use for that kind of theme.<br /> <br /> Back in 1e, blood alchemy was actually just a bunch of devotions for making what amounts to witchy potions that stored disciplines. You had to buy up a discipline that was a glorified curse power, then buy devotions that mixed the two. In 2e, you're better off just developing a scale. <br /> <br /> Scales were really great inventions to cover all the miscelanous abilities of the Ordo Dracul that were back in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:36:28-07:00","id":1114759,"title":"","content":"So I just wanted to thank everyone for the help so far, and your advice helped in the first session. (Hopefully those in my game aren't peeking.)<br /> <br /> So, I've made Coil of Zirnitra apart of the Ascendant mystery and the Coil of Ziva apart of the Wyrm mystery (I know that one is a bit odd, but I liked the interesting study in dichotomy, and I figured it would fit in with the control over one's urges that I got from the Mystery in general.) However, I figured I'd ask if these decisions were a good idea, and if not maybe some advice on altering them.<br /> <br /> For a bit more information on the chronicle in general; I choose New York, New York as the location of the setting, and each covenant rules one of the five boroughs. I picked Staten Island for the Ordo Dracul (though maybe I should have picked a different borough for them). Now, I plan to introduce the other covenants later down the line, but I figured I would ask for some advice on building mysteries for the coterie to go after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:10:54-07:00","id":1115247,"title":"","content":"Sharing an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1098658-city-concept-ruled-by-ordo-dracul?p=1099840#post1099840\">idea </a>I previously shared. It may be applicable for Staten Island, maybe not. And lets not forget<a href=\"https://the-line-up.com/cropsey-monster-of-staten-island\" target=\"_blank\"> real life</a> terror and <a href=\"http://www.urbanghostsmedia.com/2014/07/10-creepiest-phantoms-urban-legends-new-york-city/\" target=\"_blank\">urban legends</a> of that location. Have Fun!<br /> <br /> Personally I'd have Mole People be Horrors as per CofD, based on the Underdwellers from <i>Innocents</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-12-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:20:17-07:00","id":1115842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1111333-ordo-dracul-chronicle?p=1115247#post1115247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sharing an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1098658-city-concept-ruled-by-ordo-dracul?p=1099840#post1099840\">idea </a>I previously shared. It may be applicable for Staten Island, maybe not. And lets not forget<a href=\"https://the-line-up.com/cropsey-monster-of-staten-island\" target=\"_blank\"> real life</a> terror and <a href=\"http://www.urbanghostsmedia.com/2014/07/10-creepiest-phantoms-urban-legends-new-york-city/\" target=\"_blank\">urban legends</a> of that location. Have Fun!<br /> <br /> Personally I'd have Mole People be Horrors as per CofD, based on the Underdwellers from <i>Innocents</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the links! Yeah, I like picking real cities for my settings so I can draw on urban legends and stories for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:33:34-07:00","id":1115844,"title":"","content":"Alright, seeing as the vampire book doesn't have anything for ephemeral entities, this is what I've come up with for Kindred interacting with them. Summoning and exorcism work as described in the Blue Core Book since the Kindred condition doesn't really interfere with it at all. <br /> <br /> However, since Abjuration does have to be modified a bit, I have working the ritual in a way that channels the Kindred's dirge provide a plus two dice bonus, while working the ritual in a manner that channels the Kindred's Mask will penalize the dice pool by two dice. I was thinking, but I couldn't figure out whether I should allow high humanity kindred to get the bonus like high integrity, but I really don't think that quite fits.<br /> <br /> On the Wyrm's Nests situation, I'm still not entirely sure how to have the coterie interact with them, or what rituals the Ordo is supposed to work there (from a mechanical perspective I know of the Wrym's Nests merits from secrets of the Covenants, I'm just not sure how to explain to my players how said merits work in the story).<br /> <br /> I was also hoping to have the Ordo (and possibly other covenants) make use of mortal occultists, so are there any good mortal occult magics I can make use of? I know of second sight, but I wasn't sure if 2e had anything yet. If anything, they might also help me provide a better avenue for my players to interact with Wyrm's Nests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:37:31-07:00","id":1115898,"title":"","content":"I've posted this in the plot hooks thread and I'm copy/pasting here so please forgive anything a should have edited out.<br /> Invigorating Heartblood.<br /> Prerequisite Coil: The Vast Dynasty.<br /> Procedure: The Dragon extracts blood directly from his heart using a pump and his own will. Atempting the prosess courses one Agrivated Damage and each roll costs one Willpower.<br /> Roll Resolve+Stamina with a target number of 5 but subtract 1 die for each roll after the first, for each success one Vitai is extracted by the pump, when extracted the Vitai lasts one night pre point of Blood Potency of the vampire and losses one point of Blood Potency per night. The vampire does not have to use all his successes and most stop at 5 Vitai.<br /> Outcome: Known uses so far include: when injected into the heart of a Revrent roll Blood Potency and uplift as an embrace would on a pass, if fed to a human or ghoul it grants the ghoul state for a number of months equal to Blood Potency with no other costs after which the ghoul may mentain the state as normal, when injected into the heart of a vampire in torpor the vampire will awaken on a success on a roll of combined Blood Potency of the the sample and the torpored vampire, finally the sample is still Vitai but does not course Blood Bond or Addiction and allows anyone who drinks it to learn Disciplines as though they were being trained by the doner for a number of months equal to Blood Potency.<br /> This creates the possibility of granting loved ones immortality or feeding elders without forming Vinculum.<br /> I know it's very flexible but making it cost an Agrivated damage and lots of Vitai should balance things out. I also have ideas for 2 Mystery Cults connected to the Ordo if your interested, one is a Ghoul and Blood Doll running group (Voivode) and the other is a day riding biker gang (Ascendant as if I needed to tell you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}